  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116216",
      "title": "Working with Signals",
      "lectureOrder": 212,
      "videoOrder": 203,
      "sourceHash": "d7c78c31bd93b35ecf878104e35c39fdcb05733d16071dd878a3c7af2287dca2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.857,
          "end": 2.04,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] Okay, so we got started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.08,
          "en": "with setting up an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.08,
          "end": 7.62,
          "en": "with the interval function, and we added an operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.62,
          "end": 11.37,
          "en": "And this, as I mentioned, is a concept we'll see again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.37,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "a little bit later in the course when we work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 17.163,
          "en": "with some observables that are built into Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.33,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "Now, you might recall that you don't just have observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 24.36,
          "en": "but you also have subjects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.36,
          "end": 27.45,
          "en": "And subjects, as I mentioned, are observables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.45,
          "end": 31.92,
          "en": "The key difference in the end just is that with subjects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.92,
          "end": 35.94,
          "en": "you also take care of emitting those values manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.94,
          "end": 38.1,
          "en": "So there you don't just subscribe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.1,
          "end": 40.38,
          "en": "but you also emit the values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.38,
          "end": 42.24,
          "en": "Whereas with observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.24,
          "end": 45.48,
          "en": "you typically have some data source like an interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.48,
          "end": 48.18,
          "en": "that emits values automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.18,
          "end": 51.27,
          "en": "or that produces values automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 53.46,
          "en": "That's one important difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.46,
          "end": 58.14,
          "en": "But in the end, subjects are special kinds of observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.14,
          "end": 60.72,
          "en": "therefore, because you still subscribe to them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.72,
          "end": 64.35,
          "en": "and you still can subscribe to one and the same subject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.35,
          "end": 67.11,
          "en": "in different places in different Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.11,
          "end": 69.12,
          "en": "for example, if you need to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.12,
          "end": 71.13,
          "en": "Now, you might also recall though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.13,
          "end": 74.97,
          "en": "that at least in modern Angular versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.97,
          "end": 78.78,
          "en": "you also have a built-in concept called Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.78,
          "end": 81.78,
          "en": "which, unlike observables, is not coming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.78,
          "end": 83.31,
          "en": "from a third party library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.31,
          "end": 87,
          "en": "like the observable related functions are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87,
          "end": 89.67,
          "en": "but which instead are built into Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.67,
          "end": 92.37,
          "en": "And therefore, I now wanna use a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.37,
          "end": 95.78999999999999,
          "en": "and then explore the differences and similarities",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.78999999999999,
          "end": 98.78999999999999,
          "en": "and also how you can convert a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.78999999999999,
          "end": 102.33,
          "en": "to an observable and vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.33,
          "end": 105.12,
          "en": "So I got my interval observable here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.12,
          "end": 110.12,
          "en": "Now, to use a Signal, I wanna hook up this button here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.43,
          "end": 114.81,
          "en": "So my idea is to add a method in this app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 117.36,
          "en": "I'll name it onClick, the name is up to you though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.32,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "And this method should be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 120.87,
          "en": "when the button is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.87,
          "end": 124.41,
          "en": "and therefore I'll add this click event binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.41,
          "end": 127.593,
          "en": "and trigger this onClick method I just added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.48,
          "end": 132.813,
          "en": "And with that, I then wanna create a Signal here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.92,
          "end": 138.153,
          "en": "and I'll name it, clickCount,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 141.24,
          "en": "and create it with this Signal function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.24,
          "end": 142.82999999999998,
          "en": "that's provided by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 146.57999999999998,
          "en": "and that's the offer imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.57999999999998,
          "end": 150.363,
          "en": "And I'll give this Signal an initial value of zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 156.6,
          "en": "Now, of course, in onClick we can use this clickCount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.6,
          "end": 160.62,
          "en": "and update or set that Signal value, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.62,
          "end": 163.35,
          "en": "by calling the update function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.35,
          "end": 165.72,
          "en": "And we'll get the previous count here as an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.72,
          "end": 168.6,
          "en": "to this function that we have to pass to update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.6,
          "end": 170.94,
          "en": "and we can then return the new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.94,
          "end": 172.95,
          "en": "that should be set to that Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.95,
          "end": 175.17000000000002,
          "en": "So for example, prevCount plus one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.17000000000002,
          "end": 177.03300000000002,
          "en": "to update that clickCount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.71,
          "end": 182.61,
          "en": "Well, and then we can of course also output that value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.61,
          "end": 185.313,
          "en": "for example, here in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.3,
          "end": 187.923,
          "en": "clickCount like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.88,
          "end": 191.073,
          "en": "as you learned it before in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.54,
          "end": 194.85,
          "en": "In addition, we can of course also go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.85,
          "end": 196.92000000000002,
          "en": "to our component function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.92000000000002,
          "end": 200.46,
          "en": "and also, for example, set up an Effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.46,
          "end": 202.98,
          "en": "with help of the constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.98,
          "end": 205.44,
          "en": "by calling the effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.44,
          "end": 208.743,
          "en": "which is also imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.21,
          "end": 212.55,
          "en": "And to that function, we then pass a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.55,
          "end": 215.97,
          "en": "which will automatically be re-executed by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.97,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "whenever any Signal you use in here updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 223.743,
          "en": "So here we could console.log, Clicked button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.67000000000002,
          "end": 227.73,
          "en": "and then I wanna output the number of times I clicked it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.73,
          "end": 230.1,
          "en": "So I'll convert this to a template literal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.1,
          "end": 232.07999999999998,
          "en": "by using backticks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.07999999999998,
          "end": 234.93,
          "en": "so that I can inject the clickCount like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 236.19299999999998,
          "en": "into this string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.96,
          "end": 240.483,
          "en": "this.clickCount to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.77,
          "end": 245.43,
          "en": "And I'll then say, times thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.43,
          "end": 249.333,
          "en": "so that we output Clicked button X times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.49,
          "end": 252.87,
          "en": "In addition, to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.87,
          "end": 255.21,
          "en": "that we don't have too much console output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.21,
          "end": 256.89,
          "en": "I'll actually clean up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.89,
          "end": 260.01,
          "en": "or comment out this interval observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.01,
          "end": 262.983,
          "en": "so that we're not getting any log messages from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.08,
          "end": 266.67,
          "en": "With that, if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.67,
          "end": 269.853,
          "en": "I initially see Clicked button zero times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.75,
          "end": 272.49,
          "en": "but if I then click this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.49,
          "end": 274.53,
          "en": "the number here in the template updates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.53,
          "end": 278.01,
          "en": "and, of course, this output here also updates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 278.01,
          "end": 281.55,
          "en": "or we're seeing new outputs, to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.55,
          "end": 284.88,
          "en": "So, that's working as expected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 284.88,
          "end": 288,
          "en": "And of course, if you now take a closer look at this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288,
          "end": 291.65999999999997,
          "en": "this also looks like a stream of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 291.65999999999997,
          "end": 293.97,
          "en": "especially like a stream of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 293.97,
          "end": 297.27,
          "en": "that could have been produced with help of a subject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 297.27,
          "end": 300.48,
          "en": "since we're essentially emitting new values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 300.48,
          "end": 303.33,
          "en": "by calling update ourselves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 303.33,
          "end": 307.83,
          "en": "So, what's the difference compared to an observable then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 307.83,
          "end": 311.133,
          "en": "and where are maybe also some similarities?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
